  concept: 'Authored objective: Route 48 traces, plate 10 vias and fit W049.

    Authored
    requirement: Route the 48 specified traces through the original pads and ten
    vias. Install W049 as the separate 36th part.

    General teaching principle:
    PCB acceptance depends on the authored footprints, nets, layers, clearances and
    route constraints; visual appearance alone is insufficient.

    Only fresh,
    authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A multilayer road map helps visualize routing, but electrical continuity
    and constraints still require checks.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A visually connected trace is not proof of correct net connectivity
    or clearance.
